{"type":"message","id":"1617773a","parentId":"64e4e1e8","timestamp":"2026-02-26T03:32:44.728Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"                  大王，**MCP专用插件版本已经创建完成！** 🎉\n\n## ✅ **完成的内容**\n\n### 📦 **新插件创建**\n- **名称**：`autoclaw-mcp-specific`（MCP专用版本）\n- **位置**：`~/.openclaw/skills/claw-browser/autoclaw-mcp-specific/`\n\n### 🔧 **主要修改**\n\n#### 1. **manifest.json**\n- 名称改为：`autoclaw-mcp`\n- 版本号：`1.0.0-mcp` \n- 描述：专为MCP服务器设计\n- 显示名称：`autoclaw-mcp - MCP浏览器控制`\n\n#### 2. **连接配置**\n- **固定端口**：`49666`（不可配置）\n- 移除用户端口设置选项\n- 硬编码连接MCP服务器\n\n#### 3. **界面优化**\n- 移除端口配置表单\n- 简化配置页面\n- 专注于MCP功能\n\n### 🎯 **用户使用**\n\n#### 安装MCP专用版：\n1. 打开`chrome://extensions/`\n2. 加载已解压的扩展\n3. 选择`autoclaw-mcp-specific`文件夹\n4. 点击扩展图标授权即可\n\n#### 特点：\n- ✅ **无需配置**：安装即用\n- ✅ **专专用**：只连接MCP服务器\n- ✅ **简单**：没有复杂的端口设置\n- ✅ **稳定**：固定架构，减少错误\n\n### 🔄 **版本对比**\n\n| 功能 | 通用版 | MCP专用版 |\n|------|--------|-----------|\n| 端口配置 | 可配置 | 固定49666 |\n| 架构选择 | 支持两种 | 仅MCP模式 |\n| 使用复杂度 | 需要配置 | 安装即用 |\n| 目标用户 | 高级用户 | 普通用户 |\n\n大王，MCP专用插件已经准备好了！用户现在可以根据需求选择安装哪个版本，享受更简单可靠的使用体验。🔥"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v3.1","usage":{"input":111907,"output":436,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":112343,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1772076702655}}
{"type":"compaction","id":"5b60dd8f","parentId":"1617773a","timestamp":"2026-02-26T03:35:35.913Z","summary":"## Goal\n- Optimize autoclaw browser automation extension UI/UX (real-time countdown, simplified auth flow)\n- Fix page navigation behavior (current tab vs new tab issue)\n- Test MCP server connectivity and extension functionality\n- Implement bookmark management functionality through MCP tools\n- Ensure MCP server and browser extension use consistent port (18790)\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Real-time countdown display with color differentiation\n- Simplified authorization flow without redundant confirmation dialogs\n- Clear visual distinction between auth button and status display\n- Keep existing \"open mode\" settings (current tab/new tab) despite limited functional difference\n- Avoid destructive changes that break existing functionality\n- Add comprehensive documentation for user expectation management\n- Maintain both Chinese and English UI text\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Added real-time countdown system in popup.js and options.js\n- [x] Simplified auth flow by removing confirmation dialog from options.js/options.html\n- [x] Fixed TypeScript compilation errors in MCP server (index.ts syntax errors)\n- [x] Enhanced UI with orange confirm button styling and red countdown text\n- [x] Successfully built and started MCP server on port 18789\n- [x] Fixed tabId determination logic in background.js to prioritize active tab for Target.createTarget\n- [x] Modified MCP server to convert tool calls to actual CDP commands instead of mock responses\n- [x] Restored confirmation authorization dialog UI in options.html with proper event handlers\n- [x] Added detailed documentation explaining feature boundaries and usage examples\n- [x] Implemented bookmark management CDP commands in both MCP server and browser extension\n- [x] Standardized all components to use port 18790 consistently\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Testing page navigation behavior (current tab vs new tab issue)\n- [ ] Verifying WebSocket connectivity between extension and MCP server\n- [ ] Testing the complete flow with actual browser extension installation and authorization\n\n### Blocked\n- OpenClaw Gateway cannot start due to system memory issues (out of memory errors)\n- Browser control service unavailable (blocked hostname/internal IP error)\n- Port 18790 frequently gets occupied by other processes, requiring manual process termination\n- Browser control service unavailable for direct browser automation testing\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Real-time countdown**: Replaced static time display with dynamic updating every second for better user experience\n- **Simplified auth flow**: Removed redundant confirmation dialog to reduce user steps from 4 to 2\n- **Color differentiation**: Used orange (#FF5722) for auth buttons and red (#ef4444) for countdown text to prevent confusion\n- **Maintain current tab/new tab setting**: Despite limited practical difference, keep the option for user preference and consistency\n- **Add comprehensive documentation**: Rather than complex intent analysis, use clear documentation to manage user expectations\n- **Use Chrome bookmarks API**: Implement bookmark operations using native chrome.bookmarks API rather than custom solutions\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Investigate and fix page navigation behavior (current tab vs new tab)\n2. Test WebSocket connection between extension and MCP server (ws://127.0.0.1:18790/extension)\n3. Resolve OpenClaw Gateway memory issues to enable full testing\n4. Install and test the optimized browser extension\n5. Test complete installation and authorization flow with actual browser extension\n6. Verify page navigation works correctly according to open mode settings\n7. Test bookmark management functionality (search, open, create, delete)\n8. Monitor MCP server stability and address port conflict issues\n9. Conduct user acceptance testing for the restored confirmation dialog\n\n## Critical Context\n- MCP server running at: ws://127.0.0.1:18790/extension (changed from 18789 due to conflicts)\n- Gateway token: Q0hpK2oV4F9tlwbYX3RELxiJNGDvayr8OPqZzkfs\n- Modified files:\n  - ~/.openclaw/skills/claw-browser/autoclaw/popup.js (real-time countdown)\n  - ~/.openclaw/skills/claw-browser/autoclaw/options.js (simplified auth flow, event handlers)\n  - ~/.openclaw/skills/claw-browser/autoclaw/options.html (removed confirm dialog, UI restoration, documentation)\n  - ~/.openclaw/skills/claw-browser/autoclaw-mcp/src/index.ts (fixed syntax errors, tool conversion)\n  - ~/.openclaw/skills/claw-browser/autoclaw/background.js (tabId logic, bookmark handlers)\n- OpenClaw Gateway configuration: ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json\n- Original files backed up in autoclaw-broken directory\n\n---\n\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\n\n## Goal\nList all bookmarks containing \"即梦\" from the Chrome bookmarks\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- (none)\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Located Chrome bookmarks file at C:\\Users\\lenovo\\AppData\\Local\\Google\\Chrome\\User Data\\Default\\Bookmarks\n- [x] Retrieved full bookmark structure using PowerShell commands\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Searching for bookmarks containing \"即梦\" text\n\n### Blocked\n- MCP server connection failing due to WebSocket missing token parameter\n- Initial tools command failed with \"unknown command 'tools'\"\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Switched to direct file system access**: MCP tools were unavailable, so used PowerShell to access bookmarks file directly\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Parse the retrieved bookmark JSON data\n2. Search all bookmark names and URLs for \"即梦\" matches\n3. Return formatted list of matching bookmarks\n\n## Critical Context\n- Bookmarks file location: C:\\Users\\lenovo\\AppData\\Local\\Google\\Chrome\\User Data\\Default\\Bookmarks\n- Bookmark data structure contains folders with children arrays containing url objects with name/url properties\n- Multiple bookmark folders exist including \"openclaw\" folder with recent addit